cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Legacy Device Revival: Orphaned Device Reverse Engineering (HeKai/HK, Anyka AK3918, Tesco Hudl 2, KAWA & GeekMagic)"
message: >-
  If you use these protocol notes or tools in your own work, please cite this
  repository. If you build on a specific finding, cite the repository and the
  document (e.g. docs/time2-mip12/PROTOCOL.md).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Parcell"
    given-names: "Ben"
    alias: "punkpar"
    website: "https://github.com/punkpar"
repository-code: "https://github.com/punkpar/legacy-device-revival"
abstract: >-
  Protocol documentation, original tooling and Home Assistant integrations for
  cheap and end-of-life devices with no local API and no vendor support. Covers
  the Time2 MIP12 IP camera (HeKai/HK P2P protocol, including WiFi provisioning),
  the Anyka AK3918 PTZ ("V380 clone", SD-card unlock + hardening), the Tesco
  Hudl 2 tablet (rooted without a bootloader unlock via run-as + Dirty COW, with
  the SELinux/capability ceiling documented), the KAWA MINI 3 Pro dashcam
  (SigmaStar: unauthenticated RTSP, root shell and HTTP filesystem), and the
  GeekMagic SmallTV-Ultra weather clock (ESP8266 HTTP API). Structured so further
  orphaned hardware (Android boxes, smartwatches, IoT gadgets) can be documented
  the same way.
keywords:
